id: pm-rl-yi7j
title: "Recursive self-improvement: a training loop whose every generation is tracked, gated, and invalidatable"
description: "pm-rl must be able to run a policy that improves itself: a generation collects trajectories, trains a successor, and the successor collects the next generation's trajectories. The loop is easy to run and almost impossible to trust, because every property that makes a result meaningful degrades silently as it turns. The generating policy is not recorded, so nobody can say which model produced a trajectory. The held-out set quietly becomes training data, so the score rises while capability does not. The proxy objective and the objective the programme actually cares about drift apart, and only the proxy is measured. An environment or reward edit invalidates every downstream generation, and nothing says so. None of these are training problems. They are all provenance problems, which is to say context problems, and pm already models the graph that answers them. This epic makes a generation a first-class tracked item whose parent is the generation that produced its training data, makes promotion a gated transition that refuses on contamination rather than warning about it, measures the proxy-to-held-out gap across generations as the reward-hacking signal it is, and binds the whole loop to an approved generation budget that the CLI will not advance past on its own."
type: Epic
status: open
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-04T20:48:53.609Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-04T20:48:53.609Z"
author: claude
estimated_minutes: 5400
acceptance_criteria: "A generation records its base checkpoint, generating policy, collection runs and training config as typed fields; promotion refuses when the evaluation set is reachable from the candidate's training data in the dependency graph; the proxy-to-held-out gap is reported per generation and its trend across the chain; advancing past the approved generation budget is refused and names the approval item required; an environment or reward-spec edit invalidates every downstream generation transitively; 100 percent line, branch, function and docstring coverage"
